&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;61&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;This is a&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;remote role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Focus On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SEO &amp;amp; Organic Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Chowbus&#39;s SEO roadmap, including keyword strategy, technical SEO audits, site structure, and page speed/Core Web Vitals improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run competitive SEO analysis against Toast, Square, Clover, and Menusifu to find content and ranking opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the content team to brief, optimize, and publish SEO-driven blog posts, landing pages, and city- or cuisine-specific pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor rankings, organic traffic, and backlink profile using tools like Google Search Console, SEMrush, or Ahrefs, and report on progress monthly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Website &amp;amp; CMS Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day management of Chowbus&#39;s website CMS, including page builds, edits, navigation, and content governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch and maintain landing pages for campaigns, product launches, and events, working with design and demand generation partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run A/B tests on key pages (homepage, demo request forms, pricing) to improve conversion rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain site performance, uptime, and technical hygiene, partnering with engineering as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards in GA4, Tableau, or similar tools to track website traffic, campaign performance, and lead-to-demo conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track the digital marketing funnel from first touch to booked demo, in partnership with Sales and RevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver monthly and quarterly performance reports with clear takeaways and recommendations for marketing leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with RevOps and Sales to keep lead data clean and consistent across the website, CRM, and marketing automation platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid Search (Google Ads / PPC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, launch, and manage Google Ads campaigns (Search, Display, Performance Max) to drive qualified demo requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the paid search budget, bidding strategy, and keyword lists. Optimize continuously for cost per lead and ROAS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and test ad copy, landing pages, and offers to improve click-through and conversion rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Marketing Campaigns Manager so paid search complements paid social and ABM efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in digital marketing, with hands-on ownership of SEO, website/CMS, analytics, and paid search (Google Ads).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience improving organic search rankings and traffic using tools like Google Search Console, SEMrush, or Ahrefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing a CMS (WordPress, Webflow, or similar), including landing page builds and site edits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Google Analytics (GA4) and building reporting dashboards (Looker or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a paid search budget and reporting on ROAS and cost per lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional or fluent proficiency in Mandarin Chinese. Most of our team and many of our restaurant&amp;nbsp;partners communicate in Mandarin, so this skill helps you collaborate effectively and understand our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Communications, or a related field, or equivalent work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in restaurant technology, POS, payments, fintech, or another B2B SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth startup or scale-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with HubSpot, Salesforce, or a similar CRM/marketing automation platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic HTML/CSS knowledge for CMS edits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid Short-Term Disability (STD)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid AD&amp;amp;D Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Birthday off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off (PTO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The salary for this role is $80,000–$130,000, depending on experience.&amp;nbsp; This role may also be eligible for a performance bonus.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
